      "q": "4. An edge of a variable cube is increasing at the rate of $3\\;{\\text{cm}}/{\\text{s}}$. How fast is the volume of the cube increasing when the edge is $10\\;{\\text{cm}}$ long?",
      "a": "Let the length and the volume of the cube respectively be $x$ and $V$.\n$V = {x^3}$\n$\\therefore \\dfrac{{dV}}{{dt}} = \\dfrac{d}{{dt}}\\left( {{x^3}} \\right) = \\dfrac{d}{{dx}}\\left( {{x^3}} \\right)\\dfrac{{dx}}{{dt}}$\n$= 3{x^2}\\dfrac{{dx}}{{dt}}$\n$\\dfrac{{dx}}{{dt}} = 3\\;{\\text{cm}}/{\\text{s}}$\n$\\therefore \\dfrac{{dV}}{{dt}} = 3{x^2}(3) = 9{x^2}$\nSo, when $x = 10\\;{\\text{cm}}$,\n$\\dfrac{{dV}}{{dt}} = 9{(10)^2} = 900\\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}/{\\text{s}}$"
